WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.920
If you have acute
coronary syndrome,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.350
you have one or more
conditions caused

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.400
by a blockage of blood
flow to your heart muscle.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.640
This is a medical
emergency, because you

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.100
may be having a heart attack,
a condition in which your heart

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.770
muscle begins to die.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.140
Your heart is a
muscular organ that

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.500
pumps blood
containing the oxygen

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.410
and nutrients your body needs.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.790
The main pumping chamber of your
heart is the left ventricle.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.090
When your left
ventricle contracts,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.930
it sends oxygen-rich
blood to your body

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:50.590
through a large artery
called the aorta.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.590
Connected to your aorta
are small arteries

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:56.340
called coronary arteries.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.990
Blood flows from your aorta,
through the coronary arteries,

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.090
to supply your heart muscle
with oxygen and nutrients.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.880
If you have acute
coronary syndrome,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.300
blood flow through
your coronary arteries

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.930
is severely reduced
or completely blocked.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:19.780
One possible cause of reduced
blood flow is atherosclerosis.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.140
In this condition, a
build-up of a fatty substance

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.600
called plaque can narrow
your coronary arteries.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.240
If this plaque
ruptures, a blood clot

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.180
can form and block the artery.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.530
A blood clot is the
most common cause

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:39.030
of coronary artery blockage.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.090
Other, less common causes
of reduced blood flow

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:47.820
include coronary artery
spasm or dissection.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.720
In a coronary artery
spasm, triggers

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.860
such as drugs, smoking, cold
weather, and extreme stress

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:00.290
or emotions can cause a
temporary and sudden tightening

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:01.495
of a coronary artery.

00:02:01.495 --> 00:02:04.640
 

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.170
During a coronary
artery dissection,

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.080
the inside wall of one
of your coronary arteries

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.555
separates, which can
block blood flow.

00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:16.110
 

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.410
Regardless of the
cause, a blockage

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.660
in either coronary
artery prevents

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.090
the oxygen and
nutrients in your blood

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:27.540
from reaching the part of your
heart supplied by the artery.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.600
As a result, heart muscle
in that area starts to die.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.630
Death of part of
your heart muscle

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.660
is called a heart attack.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.240
It's also known as a
myocardial infarction or MI.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.510
A blocked coronary
artery may also

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:49.770
cause you to feel sudden
pain, discomfort, tightening,

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:54.880
or a burning sensation in
your chest called angina.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:00.320
This pain may extend to your
upper abdomen, shoulders, arms,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.065
neck, and lower jaw.

00:03:02.065 --> 00:03:05.160
 

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.710
If you have angina
when you're at rest,

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.100
or frequent angina
that prevents even

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.350
moderate physical activity,
you have unstable angina,

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.305
which is the main symptom
of acute coronary syndrome.

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:20.250
 

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.890
Other symptoms of
acute coronary syndrome

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:28.890
include shortness of
breath, dizziness, nausea,

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.560
and sweating.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.780
 

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.980
If you've had a
heart attack or have

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.810
other types of acute
coronary syndrome,

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.630
your doctor may
prescribe oxygen therapy

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.855
to get more oxygen
into your blood.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.360
 

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.550
You may take aspirin or other
prescription blood-thinner

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:52.510
drugs to prevent blood clots.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:56.260
Thrombolytics also known
as clot-buster drugs,

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.435
may be used to break up
any existing blood clots.

00:03:59.435 --> 00:04:03.430
 

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.700
Drugs such as
nitroglycerin and morphine

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.040
will relax your
coronary arteries

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.895
and relieve the pain of angina.

00:04:10.895 --> 00:04:15.870
 

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:19.110
You may also receive drugs
called beta blockers that

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.270
slow down your heart and
reduce its need for oxygen.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.430
 

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:30.310
Your doctor may also recommend
immediate surgical procedures,

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.900
such as coronary angioplasty, in
which a balloon-tipped catheter

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.410
inflates inside your blocked
coronary artery to open it.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.760
 

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.000
may leave behind a mesh-like
device called a stent

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.300
 

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.700
After inflating, the balloon catheter
 may leave behind

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:57.200
a mesh-like device called a stent 
to hold your artery open.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:05.200
Or you may have a coronary
artery bypass graft, or CABG.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.990
CABG is a surgical
procedure in which the blocked

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.400
areas of the coronary arteries

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.600
are bypassed with veins or
artificial graft material.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.900
Seek treatment
immediately if you

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.700
have the symptoms of
acute coronary syndrome.

